WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
Hey there, welcome to Models and Agents for Beginners, episode 71.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.460
It's June 14th, 2026.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:10.680
Let's break down today as coolest AI news so anyone can understand it.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:11.280
Let's go!

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:12.740
Picture this.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.140
You snap a group photo at a concert, but the edge cuts off half the stage.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:22.760
Instead of tossing the shot, your phone could soon add new scenery on any side to rescue it.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.940
That is the new Extend feature coming to iPhones with iOS 27.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.300
Think of it like auto-complete on your phone keyboard,

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:35.240
except the guesses fill in missing parts of a picture rather than words.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:40.000
The system studies the colors, shapes, and patterns already in your photo

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.320
then continues those patterns outward in a way that usually feels natural.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:49.080
It works on the top, bottom, left, or right so you can fix a crop horizon

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.240
or make a tight selfie feel more open.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.340
Almost every teen takes and shares photos daily,

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:59.300
so this removes a tiny but annoying limit on creative sharing or school projects.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:03.600
When the update lands, you simply open the Photos app, pick an image,

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.360
drag the new Extend handles and watch the blank space fill in right away.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:10.900
No extra apps or accounts are required.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:17.060
The real magic happens because the AI treats the photo like a puzzle where it already knows most of the

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:21.980
pieces. It predicts what the missing pieces should look like based on everything it has learned

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:27.620
from millions of other images. That same idea of guessing what comes next powers many tools

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.860
we use every day, from texting to music recommendations.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:35.540
And that is basically how the Extend feature works, not so scary right.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:41.100
One way to picture the prediction step is to imagine a painter who only sees the left half of

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:45.060
a landscape, but still finishes the right half so it matches perfectly.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:50.440
Another angle is a jigsaw puzzle where the AI does not just copy pieces,

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:53.900
it invents new ones that keep the same lighting and style.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:59.740
A third view is like a band that hears the first verse of a song and then keeps playing in the

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:05.640
exact same rhythm and mood. These layers show why the results often look natural instead of

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:11.080
obviously added. Apple's image playground also received major updates this week.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:16.620
The refresh tool upgrades from rigid voice commands to a system that can chat back and forth

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:22.980
while remembering earlier context. It combines smaller on-device models with larger cloud models

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:28.160
for added power when needed. Most users already rely on Siri for timers and messages,

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:33.320
so the conversational shift could reshape daily phone interactions during homework or planning.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:37.440
The features are slated for fall release on compatible iPhones.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:43.160
ArsTechnica noted the change moves AI from a separate app into a built-in companion.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:48.580
This development continues Apple's ongoing push to embed smarter assistants directly

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:56.100
in hardware people carry every day. OpenAI expanded free-tier image generation in chat GPT,

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.720
giving non-paying users more creation power without upgrades.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:06.320
K-pop fans responded by highlighting realistic deep-fake videos and images made without consent.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:12.720
These fakes often place idols in awkward or misleading scenes that spread quickly on social platforms.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:17.420
Reddit threads documented the calls for better detection tools and awareness.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:23.680
The episode stressed that spotting AI media is turning into a routine skill for everyday scrolling.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:30.580
One practical step is comparing suspect images side-by-side with verified photos on trusted sites.

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:37.140
This thread shows how rapid image tools create both creative access and new moderation challenges.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:42.280
Okay, now for my favorite part of the show where we turn that understanding into action

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:48.920
you can take right now. First up is a free tool from Deezer that scans playlist on Spotify or Apple

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:56.100
Music to flag tracks made by AI. More music online is created by computers and many listeners want to

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:03.140
know what is human-made versus machine-made. Go to the Deezer website, find the AI detector tool,

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:06.760
paste a playlist link from another service, and see what it flags.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:13.380
Next, DoorDash added an AI chatbot that lets you order food by typing a description or even

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:19.660
snapping a photo of a menu. The chatbot reads the photo or your words and turns them into an order

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:24.700
without you scrolling through endless options. Try it by opening the DoorDash app,

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:29.900
tapping the chat option, and either typing what you want or uploading a picture of a dish you

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:35.840
saw online. Finally, Google released live speech-to-speech translation that works almost

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:41.300
instantly during video calls. Think of it like having a super fast interpreter in your pocket

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:46.680
who listens, understands, and speaks the translation while the first person is still talking.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:51.820
It keeps the original speaker's tone and rhythm so the voice still sounds like the same person.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:57.060
Students could practice conversations with people around the world without waiting for subtitles.

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:03.020
To try the translation side, keep an eye on Google Apps this summer and test it during a call with

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:07.940
a friend who speaks another language. Here are a few quick bits that caught my eye this week.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:15.180
One AI researcher suggests saving your hardest or most unusual ideas now because AI is making a

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:21.580
cheaper to turn good ideas into finished projects. The bottleneck is shifting from how do I build this

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:28.020
to what should I build? Just a year ago, the most advanced AI helpers could only answer questions.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:34.080
Today they can take actions across multiple tools, which is exciting, but also means we need to think

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:40.200
carefully about safety as they get more powerful. A separate report found that some image tools are

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:46.000
still hosting problematic deep-fake images even after earlier complaints, which shows why learning

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:52.160
to spot AI-generated media is becoming an everyday skill. You can practice by searching for AI

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:57.900
deep-fake examples on a trusted site and comparing them side by side with real photos to train your

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:05.200
eye. Visa is testing connections between its payment system and Chad GPT so AI agents can eventually

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:11.140
complete purchases with user permission. The effort remains early yet signals how financial firms

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:17.700
are preparing for agents that handle routine buying. Mistral is reportedly moving away from frontier

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:23.620
model development toward contractor style work according to recent posts. Related commentary

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:29.380
notes that non-key tasks may gain the most from stronger models, while assumptions about routing

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:35.580
simple jobs to smaller ones may be flawed. Google Earth Flight Simulation surfaced as a lighter

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:41.860
